{"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"EPUB Image Preview"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Navigator","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Preferences","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/SwiftUI","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Input","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Highlights","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Decorations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/EPUB-Fonts"],"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/EPUB-Image-Preview"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"[!IMPORTANT]","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"targetElement"},{"text":" is an experimental API gated behind a Swift SPI. You must opt in at the import site and accept that the API may change in future releases.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note"},{"anchor":"Detecting-image-taps","text":"Detecting image taps","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The EPUB Navigator populates ","type":"text"},{"code":"PointerEvent.targetElement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when it recognizes the content element under the pointer. The ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TargetElement"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" value exposes two properties:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" – the "},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ContentElement","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" under the pointer (e.g., "},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ImageContentElement","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SVGContentElement","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"frame","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" – the element’s on-screen "},{"code":"CGRect","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" relative to the navigator’s view"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":".activate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" observer (described in the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"Input.md","type":"reference"},{"text":") to react to taps and clicks, then downcast ","type":"text"},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the specific type you want to handle:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@_spi(ExperimentalTargetElement) import ReadiumNavigator","","navigator.addObserver(.activate { event in","    guard","        let targetElement = event.targetElement,","        let image = targetElement.content as? ImageContentElement","    else {","        return false","    }","    \/\/ The user tapped an image – handle it here.","    return true","})"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returning ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" consumes the event, preventing other observers from handling the same tap.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Working-with-ImageContentElement","text":"Working with `ImageContentElement`","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ImageContentElement"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" describes a bitmap image element and provides the following properties:","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Property","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Type","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Description"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"embeddedLink","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Link"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Points to the image resource in the publication","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"caption"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"String?","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Caption from the enclosing figure’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<figcaption>"},{"text":" element","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"accessibleName","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String?"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Accessible name, computed following ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/accname-1.2"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessibleDescription"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String?"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Accessible description, computed following ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"accname-1.2","type":"text"}],"overridingTitle":"accname-1.2","type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/accname-1.2"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"extendedDescriptions","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"[Link]","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Links to extended descriptions, declared with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/daisy.github.io\/transitiontoepub\/best-practices\/extended-desc\/ExtendedDescriptionsBestPractices.html","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property returns the ","type":"text"},{"code":"accessibleName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". To display a single text under the image, prefer the caption when available instead: ","type":"text"},{"code":"element.caption ?? element.accessibleName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The caption and the accessible name can be the same string, when the ","type":"text"},{"code":"<figcaption>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" also named an image which had no ","type":"text"},{"code":"alt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute. Coalesce them as above rather than concatenating them, or that image is labelled twice.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"[!NOTE]","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SVGContentElement"}]},{"text":" follows a similar shape for inline SVG (","type":"text"},{"code":"<svg>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), but exposes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"svg: String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property with the raw SVG source instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"embeddedLink","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". SVG images referenced via ","type":"text"},{"code":"<img src=\"...svg\">","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are reported as ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ImageContentElement","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Extended-descriptions","text":"Extended descriptions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the publication attaches ","type":"text"},{"overridingTitle":"extended descriptions","type":"reference","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"extended descriptions","type":"text"}],"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/daisy.github.io\/transitiontoepub\/best-practices\/extended-desc\/ExtendedDescriptionsBestPractices.html"},{"text":" to an image with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aria-details"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extendedDescriptions"},{"text":" holds one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Link"},{"text":" per description. Each link points either at a separate resource of the publication, or at the description’s container in the current resource (a fragment href). Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"text":" comes from the target’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aria-label"},{"text":" or, for hyperlink targets, its text.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A good place to surface them is the image preview itself, as a “view extended description” action per link. To display one, navigate to it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["if let link = image.extendedDescriptions.first {","    if let locator = publication.locator(for: link) {","        await navigator.go(to: locator)","","    } else if let url = link.httpURL {","        \/\/ The description lives outside the publication.","        UIApplication.shared.open(url.url)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"This guide explains how to detect when a user taps an image in an EPUB publication to present it in a dedicated view, using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"PointerEvent.targetElement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" API.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/readium\/epub-image-preview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/NavigatorOverview"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"Highlights.md":{"titleInlineContent":[{