"kind":"article","title":"Navigator Overview","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn about the architecture, configuration, and usage of the Readium Navigator."}],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/navigatoroverview","role":"article"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/SwiftUI":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/SwiftUI","kind":"article","title":"Integrating the Navigator with SwiftUI","abstract":[{"text":"The Navigator is built with UIKit and provides ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIViewController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implementations. Nevertheless, you can integrate them into a SwiftUI view hierarchy using Apple’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swiftui\/uiviewrepresentable","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/swiftui","role":"article"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Input":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Input","kind":"article","title":"Observing user input","abstract":[{"text":"In visual publications like EPUB or PDF, users can interact with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"VisualNavigator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance using gestures, a keyboard, a mouse, a pencil, or a trackpad. When the publication does not override user input events, you may want to intercept them to trigger actions in your user interface. For example, you can turn pages or toggle the navigation bar on taps, or open a bookmarks screen when pressing the Command-Shift-D hotkey.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/input","role":"article"},"https://daisy.github.io/transitiontoepub/best-practices/extended-desc/ExtendedDescriptionsBestPractices.html":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aria-details"}],"title":"aria-details","url":"https:\/\/daisy.github.io\/transitiontoepub\/best-practices\/extended-desc\/ExtendedDescriptionsBestPractices.html","identifier":"https:\/\/daisy.github.io\/transitiontoepub\/best-practices\/extended-desc\/ExtendedDescriptionsBestPractices.html","type":"link"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Preferences":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Preferences","kind":"article","title":"Configuring the Navigator","abstract":[{"text":"Take a look at the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"..\/Migration%20Guide.md","type":"reference"},{"text":" if you are already using the legacy EPUB settings.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/preferences","role":"article"},"Input.md":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Input guide"}],"title":"Input guide","url":"Input.md","identifier":"Input.md","type":"link"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/EPUB-Fonts":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/EPUB-Fonts","kind":"article","title":"Font families in the EPUB navigator","abstract":[{"text":"Readium allows users to customize the font family used to render a reflowable EPUB, by changing the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"Preferences.md","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/epub-fonts","role":"article"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Navigator":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/navigator","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Navigator","title":"Navigator","abstract":[{"text":"You can use a Readium Navigator to present the publication to the user. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Navigator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" renders resources on the screen and offers APIs and user interactions for navigating the contents.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic"},"https://www.w3.org/TR/accname-1.2":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"accname-1.2"}],"title":"accname-1.2","url":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/accname-1.2","identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/accname-1.2","type":"link"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Highlights":{"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/highlights","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Highlights","title":"Implementing Highlights","abstract":[{"text":"Highlighting lets users mark up passages in a publication for later reference - a core feature of any reading app. In Readium, highlights are built on top of the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Decoration API","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". If you want to understand that API in depth or build a custom decoration style, see the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"Decorations.md"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic"},"Decorations.md":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decorations guide"}],"title":"Decorations guide","url":"Decorations.md","identifier":"Decorations.md","type":"link"}}}